  "drumMap": "gs-standard",
  "notes": [
    "Channel 10 plays drum sets, chosen by program; the other channels play melodic sounds.",
    "The melodic names are the General MIDI program names at bank 0 (the capital tones), and the instrument's display shows Roland's own names for them.",
    "Bank select uses CC0; CC32 is ignored.",
    "Drum maps follow the drum set table of the owner's manual: the kits at programs 48, 56 and 127 have their own map, and the other kits share the standard map.",
    "The Room, Power, Electronic, TR-808 and Brush sets are listed under the standard map's names; at a few keys those sets play a different voice than the name shows (the owner's manual lists the replaced voices).",
    "Programs here are numbered 0 to 127 as sent; Roland's manual numbers them 1 to 128."
  ]
}
